tags: party_affairs

= Reunification with the <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span>

Since the Regensburg Agreement, our relationship with the once estranged <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span> has mostly normalised, especially with the delineation of our explicit spheres of influence. Despite that, pressure still remains at the grassroots level for the reformation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> back into a united Catholic party, with the result of the 1925 Presidential Elections a warning to many <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> members of the price of continued Catholic disunity. 
 
In light of the resignation of long-time party leader Wilhelm Marx, the onus now falls on [+ z_party_leader +] to bring the prodigal son back into the fold. With the <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span>'s demand for continued political autonomy being a sticking point, the alternative pathway to reunification lies in the establishment of a formal working relationship with the <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span> such that they can function as an official sister party of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span>. 

- @catholic_rights: ds
- @rb_distance: Resolve the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Reichbanner**</span> issue
- @fund_org: saas
- @easy_discard

@catholic_rights
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; center_strength += 5; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 5; workers_kpd -= 1.5; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 1 if dnvp_ideology == "Radical"; workers_dnf -= 1; unemployed_kpd -= 2; unemployed_nsdap -= 2; kpd_relation -= 10

Attacking the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-[? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span> is popular among all but the left wing of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the bourgeois parties. This might also hamper our ability to reconcile with the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> in the future.

